### Step 5: Calculate the angle \(\alpha\)

The angle \(\alpha\) made by the image with the principal axis can be found using the tangent of the angle, which is the ratio of the perpendicular height of the image to its longitudinal length.
\tan \alpha = \frac{\text{perpendicular height of image}}{\text{longitudinal length of image}} = \frac{h_i}{x}
